WEBVTT

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:45.720
Do you want to eat some melon?

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:50.500
It looks delicious!

00:01:50.500 --> 00:01:52.710
Hey! This is your brother's!

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:55.950
You're mean! Can't I at least have one?

00:01:55.950 --> 00:01:56.890
No.

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.350
Chiharu!

00:01:59.350 --> 00:02:03.190
The anterior talofibular ligament ruptured in the right ankle, 

00:02:03.190 --> 00:02:05.750
and the talus is broken. 

00:02:05.750 --> 00:02:08.840
The dorsal ligaments are also injured.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:13.990
It's been decided that we're going to perform surgery for the ligament tomorrow.

00:02:13.990 --> 00:02:15.430
Surgery?

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:16.630
Yes.

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:19.790
Then... will he recover in time for the summer tournament that begins two months from now...?

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:22.730
There's no way.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:25.990
It'll be a month before the cast comes off.

00:02:25.990 --> 00:02:27.790
After that, he'll undergo rehab.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:31.050
Getting back to normal life will take a month.

00:02:31.670 --> 00:02:34.540
And to get back to the level he was at,

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:37.460
it'll take at least three months.

00:02:38.440 --> 00:02:39.890
Three months?

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:41.680
Then, Goro,

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.980
we're going home for now, okay?

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.420
We'll come back tonight.

00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:47.430
Yeah.

00:02:49.030 --> 00:02:50.360
Bye, bye!

00:02:51.990 --> 00:02:54.450
Will he get better soon?

00:02:54.450 --> 00:02:56.330
I don't have a person to play catch with.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:58.350
I feel so bored!

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:00.330
That's right.

00:03:06.860 --> 00:03:08.000
Egashira!

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.150
Hey there,

00:03:10.150 --> 00:03:11.840
how are you feeling?

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.730
What did you come here for?

00:03:17.590 --> 00:03:19.360
By the looks of that,

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.900
it seems as though it wasn't just a sprain.

00:03:22.320 --> 00:03:24.980
Did you come here to check on the damage?

00:03:26.190 --> 00:03:27.630
How horrible!

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.550
Seems like you've misunderstood me.

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:34.110
Shizuka-ojousan and the others must've said something to you.

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:35.240
How troubling.

00:03:36.530 --> 00:03:39.210
It's fine. I'll tell you.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.080
After the surgery, it'll take two months to recover.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:44.940
To completely heal, at the earliest, it'll take three months.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:49.080
And, of course, I won't be able to enter in the summer tournament.

00:03:51.070 --> 00:03:52.930
There you go. Are you satisfied?

00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:56.190
That's disappointing to hear.

00:03:56.190 --> 00:03:59.210
To think that your high school life would end...

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:04.520
without you beating Kaido or even participating in an actual game.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:05.980
This is a token of my feelings.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:09.570
Please use it for your hospital bills.

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.110
Wait.

00:04:15.570 --> 00:04:16.770
Wh-

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:20.410
Isn't it a bit early to be giving that to me as a "sorry"?

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:23.900
Who said I'm not participating in the games?

00:04:23.900 --> 00:04:28.480
Did you think I'd give up because of such an injury?

00:04:29.090 --> 00:04:30.920
I'll definitely recover!

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:35.430
I won't let anyone get in my way!

00:04:36.170 --> 00:04:39.390
I-It'll take three months to completely heal!?

00:04:39.790 --> 00:04:41.050
Yes.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:46.020
We're going to have to enter the tournament without him.

00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.860
I'm sure it's a shock to everyone,

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:50.980
but let's try and carry his share as well.

00:04:51.840 --> 00:04:53.570
You're joking, right?

00:04:53.940 --> 00:04:58.200
What have we been practicing for up until now?

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:01.340
Seishuu's only hope was Shigeno.

00:05:01.340 --> 00:05:03.580
Without the ace and clean-up hitter here,

00:05:03.580 --> 00:05:07.170
how are we supposed to compete from now on?

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.270
Um... everyone...

00:05:10.270 --> 00:05:12.220
Don't you have to practice?

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:16.350
How can we practice in this condition?

00:05:16.350 --> 00:05:18.640
I'm in such shock that I'm going to be depressed.

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:22.900
We've lost all hope.

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:32.300
Hey!

00:05:33.780 --> 00:05:35.490
You guys are so heartless.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:37.700
What are you talking about?

00:05:37.700 --> 00:05:39.820
There's nothing you can do about being depressed,

00:05:39.820 --> 00:05:44.000
but why didn't you have the courage to say you're going to visit Shigeno?

00:05:45.510 --> 00:05:47.530
You don't get it, do you?

00:05:47.530 --> 00:05:50.170
Can't you think about other people's feelings?

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:51.880
"Think about other people"?

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:56.330
Just how much do you think Shigeno has riding on this tournament?

00:05:56.330 --> 00:06:00.470
And, if you consider his feelings about getting hurt at this crucial point,

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:04.430
there's nothing you can say to him!

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.350
What part of that is thinking about others!?

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.020
What?

00:06:08.530 --> 00:06:12.230
That's just you guys not wanting to see him because it's hard for you!

00:06:13.660 --> 00:06:17.900
Right now, who do you think it's the hardest on!?

00:06:28.280 --> 00:06:33.000
Forget it. If that's the case, I'll just go myself and encourage him!

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:44.960
Yes?

00:06:48.720 --> 00:06:51.930
Shimizu-san... why are you here?

00:06:51.930 --> 00:06:53.940
I heard from my little brother...

00:06:53.940 --> 00:06:56.700
that Honda injured his ligaments and was hospitalized.

00:06:57.360 --> 00:06:58.650
Well...

00:06:58.650 --> 00:07:03.380
for you, who's on the softball team, to come by and see our Shigeno,

00:07:03.380 --> 00:07:06.580
as the manager I have to thank you properly.

00:07:08.450 --> 00:07:09.990
What a pity! 

00:07:09.990 --> 00:07:12.550
You brought flowers over,

00:07:12.550 --> 00:07:14.760
but there's nowhere to put them.

00:07:19.590 --> 00:07:22.930
Hey! What are you doing? You're hurt, you know?

00:07:23.800 --> 00:07:28.200
This injury isn't that big of a deal. The surgery went well too.

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.530
Now all I have to do is fix it with my spirit.

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.780
Don't overdo it.

00:07:33.780 --> 00:07:35.980
You have a history of getting hurt.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.320
Don't be like you were in Little League,

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:43.880
when you got too focused on the fight in front of you... 

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:46.990
and damaged your body. 

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:50.160
W-Wait a second! 

00:07:50.160 --> 00:07:52.140
Darling, don't tell me that you're going to play in the tournament?

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:53.960
Of course I'm going to play.

00:07:55.320 --> 00:07:59.300
Well, I knew it'd be useless to tell you not to.

00:08:00.130 --> 00:08:01.120
See ya.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:04.380
Please take your time.

00:08:07.690 --> 00:08:09.530
Oh, that's right,

00:08:09.530 --> 00:08:12.770
instead of a vase, I have a urinal.{AMS: "urinal" is the term that is used in hospitals for it... my mom's a nurse and I asked her :p}

00:08:16.980 --> 00:08:18.510
Go, don't go.

00:08:18.510 --> 00:08:19.690
Go, don't go.

00:08:19.690 --> 00:08:20.570
All right, I'll go... or I won't.{I'll go after all? instead of "all right i'll go"? -sangofe}

00:08:20.570 --> 00:08:22.970
All right, I'll go... or I won't.{I'll go after all? instead of "all right i'll go"? -sangofe}

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:25.160
Oh, isn't that Fuji?

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:27.120
K-Kaoru-chan!

00:08:28.130 --> 00:08:29.120
Are you going to see him too?

00:08:29.120 --> 00:08:31.210
Uh... uh... y-yeah.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:34.280
Yeah, that's right, that's right... I'm going to see him.

00:08:34.280 --> 00:08:36.890
Then you should go quickly.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:39.630
That manager, Nakamura or whatever, is here too.

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:44.620
Oh... well... I don't really want to meet her...

00:08:44.620 --> 00:08:45.340
Huh?

00:08:45.770 --> 00:08:49.220
A-Anyway, how's Shigeno doing?

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:51.890
After all that's happened, isn't he depressed?

00:08:53.350 --> 00:08:56.850
Not really. Other than his leg, he seemed perfectly fine.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:59.070
R-Really?

00:08:59.610 --> 00:09:02.690
By the way, I heard from Taiga,

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:05.300
that you seem to be trying hard at practice!

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:09.050
He says that you have the loudest voice.

00:09:09.050 --> 00:09:11.640
That's incredibly important.

00:09:11.640 --> 00:09:12.460
See ya!

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:17.000
Oh, that's right.

00:09:17.880 --> 00:09:21.590
Now that the ace and clean-up batter is gone, everyone's lost their will to go on, right?

00:09:21.590 --> 00:09:25.090
Oh... um... well...

00:09:25.750 --> 00:09:27.230
But, you know what?

00:09:27.230 --> 00:09:30.050
Don't let all that hard work go to waste!

00:09:32.410 --> 00:09:33.550
Isn't it fine?

00:09:33.550 --> 00:09:38.230
You guys should display the results of your hard work, and that'll be enough!

00:09:39.690 --> 00:09:40.780
See you later!

00:09:49.990 --> 00:09:50.760
All right!

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:51.850
Let's do it!

00:09:51.850 --> 00:09:56.830
Now that Shigeno's not here, if I don't pull the team along, who will!?

00:09:57.940 --> 00:09:59.330
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:01.350
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:09:59.330 --> 00:10:01.330
Hey! What's wrong, second-years? 

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:03.230
You're not loud enough! 

00:10:01.350 --> 00:10:03.000
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:03.000 --> 00:10:04.730
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:03.230 --> 00:10:05.510
Your shouting is horrible, senpai!

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:06.430
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu! 

00:10:06.430 --> 00:10:07.470
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu! 

00:10:07.980 --> 00:10:09.670
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:08.880 --> 00:10:10.180
You're late, Fuji!

00:10:09.670 --> 00:10:11.200
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:15.960
You guys! Why are you getting all into it without my words of encouragement!?

00:10:11.200 --> 00:10:12.920
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:12.920 --> 00:10:14.620
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:14.620 --> 00:10:16.220
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:15.960 --> 00:10:18.390
Nothing good will come out of being depressed forever!

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:17.930
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:19.530
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:18.390 --> 00:10:21.400
At times like these, we have to practice! Practice!

00:10:19.530 --> 00:10:21.090
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.850
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:22.250 --> 00:10:25.980
Their first goal seems to be to win the first game.

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:24.500
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:24.500 --> 00:10:26.050
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:26.050 --> 00:10:27.780
Seishuu! Seishuu! Seishuu!

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:29.780
Where do you want to eat lunch?

00:10:29.780 --> 00:10:32.280
They're going to be sold out of fried noodles in a bun!{Let's put a note what this is (type of bread) -sangofe}

00:10:36.600 --> 00:10:40.670
But you know, Tashiro, what are we going to do about the last member?

00:10:41.050 --> 00:10:45.460
Even if we practice, with only eight members, we can't play in a game.

00:10:47.090 --> 00:10:50.870
If that's the case, I've already thought of something.

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:53.600
And I added a little enticement. 

00:10:53.600 --> 00:10:54.880
Enticement?

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:59.940
Oh, by the way, Taiga hasn't been here since this morning.

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:04.090
Oh, if you're talking about Shimizu-kun, then during lunch...

00:11:18.290 --> 00:11:19.590
He really... He really quit!?

00:11:19.590 --> 00:11:21.560
He really... He really quit!?

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:27.840
This is a free fansub.

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:27.840
Not for sale or rent.

00:11:28.420 --> 00:11:31.180
What!? You quit the baseball team!?

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:35.050
Yeah, there's no point in continuing.

00:11:35.050 --> 00:11:37.640
What do you mean, "there's no point"?

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:38.890
Don't tell me you're going to say...

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:43.690
that because of Honda's injury you've lost all your hopes and dreams!

00:11:44.240 --> 00:11:45.190
There <i>are</i> none.

00:11:46.420 --> 00:11:49.240
It's a garbage team without Shigeno Goro there.

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:51.450
What kind of hope is there?

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:56.860
I went to Seishuu because I thought that we'd be able to get somewhere with that pitcher.

00:11:56.860 --> 00:11:58.400
T-Then...

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:02.940
you're going to quit baseball after you've worked so hard at it?

00:12:02.940 --> 00:12:06.670
There're a few schools that offered me baseball scholarships before.

00:12:06.670 --> 00:12:11.110
If I ask one of them, they'll probably let me transfer.

00:12:11.110 --> 00:12:12.480
Hey, you!

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:25.600
What're you doing!?

00:12:25.600 --> 00:12:27.360
Shut the door!

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:30.740
I have such a pitiful younger brother.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:36.870
You said that practices and coaches at famous schools were annoying, so you came to Seishuu.

00:12:36.870 --> 00:12:39.400
Now that the anticipated ace is gone,

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:44.250
you want to abandon your friends and turn to a school that you rejected before?

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:46.440
Friends?

00:12:47.680 --> 00:12:50.590
I joined only a month ago, so we're not friends or anything.

00:12:51.190 --> 00:12:54.310
The situation's changed, so there's nothing I can do about it.

00:12:54.310 --> 00:12:56.430
If the team doesn't win and attract the attention of others,

00:12:56.430 --> 00:12:59.400
no one's going to scout me.

00:13:00.390 --> 00:13:03.470
Instead of staying on a team that's going to be defeated in the first round,

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:06.190
I'd rather go to a famous school.

00:13:06.800 --> 00:13:10.270
If that's the case, you should use your own strength to make Seishuu win!

00:13:11.320 --> 00:13:13.590
Just because you have a little bit of baseball sense,

00:13:13.590 --> 00:13:16.240
you look for the easy way out and try to stand out!

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:19.240
A coward who acts tough and then transfers?

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:26.250
Compared to Honda, who left an impression on Kaido before transferring to Seishuu to better himself,

00:13:26.250 --> 00:13:29.650
you're not even <i>this</i> close to being as cool as he is!

00:13:31.200 --> 00:13:37.090
I've done the team a huge injustice by introducing a younger brother like you to them!

00:13:38.730 --> 00:13:40.530
Shut up, you stupid sister!

00:13:40.530 --> 00:13:43.530
I have my own rules that I live by!

00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:50.690
Good morning, Taiga-kun!

00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:50.690
Good morning, Taiga-kun!

00:13:50.690 --> 00:13:55.780
A-Actually, we wanted to talk to you.

00:13:55.780 --> 00:13:58.950
It won't take up much of your time, so can we talk?

00:14:00.980 --> 00:14:03.180
That brat-

00:14:03.180 --> 00:14:05.160
B-Bear with it, Fuji!

00:14:04.380 --> 00:14:06.150
Oh yeah, that's right.

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:10.040
Do you want me to pitch in place of Shigeno-senpai?

00:14:13.100 --> 00:14:15.970
Then, Shimizu-kun, try throwing the ball, please.

00:14:16.550 --> 00:14:17.630
Okay.

00:14:30.360 --> 00:14:31.980
That's pretty fast!

00:14:35.220 --> 00:14:36.600
It's good, isn't it?

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:37.950
His control's not bad too.

00:14:38.670 --> 00:14:41.910
With him, it might just be enough to fight back.

00:14:41.910 --> 00:14:43.430
All right!

00:14:43.430 --> 00:14:46.280
We have to try harder too!

00:14:46.280 --> 00:14:47.070
But...

00:14:47.070 --> 00:14:49.740
we won't be able to play with eight people.

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:52.300
You're right.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.050
Excuse me?

00:14:56.090 --> 00:14:59.680
Is this where the baseball field is?

00:14:59.680 --> 00:15:00.860
Yeah, that's right.

00:15:00.860 --> 00:15:02.050
Do you need something?

00:15:02.050 --> 00:15:04.090
Um... well...

00:15:04.090 --> 00:15:07.270
I saw the team recruitment flyer and came here...

00:15:07.270 --> 00:15:10.310
B-By any chance, are you hoping to join the team?

00:15:10.310 --> 00:15:12.270
Y-Yes.

00:15:12.270 --> 00:15:17.550
H-He came! They fell for the flyers I handed out!

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:19.110
No way.

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:21.770
Thank you for coming!

00:15:21.770 --> 00:15:24.510
You... um... what's your name?

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:26.120
It's Hattori. 

00:15:26.120 --> 00:15:28.570
I see! Hattori-kun, huh?

00:15:28.570 --> 00:15:31.840
I'm the vice-captain, Fuji! I'm counting on you!

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:34.700
When did he become vice-captain?

00:15:34.700 --> 00:15:35.880
Like I'd know.

00:15:36.290 --> 00:15:43.110
I'm a very reliable guy, so if you don't understand something, feel free to ask me!

00:15:43.110 --> 00:15:44.720
Then... just one question.

00:15:45.980 --> 00:15:48.180
What's the photo at the bottom?

00:15:52.830 --> 00:15:54.300
It's my picture!

00:15:54.300 --> 00:15:56.750
What's this about, Fuji-senpai?

00:15:56.750 --> 00:16:00.190
Um... well, you see,

00:16:00.190 --> 00:16:06.770
in the world today, if that kind of enticement isn't there, people will be bored...

00:16:05.430 --> 00:16:08.670
Fuji-senpai, you're the worst!

00:16:08.170 --> 00:16:09.450
W-Wait!

00:16:10.050 --> 00:16:13.330
Well, with this, we've got our members.

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:16.420
Well then, to be prepared for the summer tournament,

00:16:16.420 --> 00:16:18.480
let's start training seriously!

00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:19.920
Yeah!

00:16:25.180 --> 00:16:26.360
Sorry about this.

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:30.390
You came to visit me but ended up helping me with my discharge procedures instead.

00:16:31.130 --> 00:16:35.150
No, not at all! I'm glad that I'm of use to you, darling!

00:16:36.320 --> 00:16:38.000
Oh... I see...

00:16:38.000 --> 00:16:41.240
But I'm glad that they're all getting into doing this.

00:16:41.810 --> 00:16:44.230
Because if there isn't a baseball team left when I recover,

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:46.460
I wouldn't be able to play in the tournament.

00:16:47.280 --> 00:16:50.020
You're seriously planning on playing in the tournament?

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:50.830
Yeah.

00:16:51.460 --> 00:16:55.060
We've got nine people, so you don't have to force yourself!

00:16:55.060 --> 00:16:57.380
Why do you want to play so much?

00:16:58.060 --> 00:17:00.200
What do you mean, "why"?

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:02.590
Because I like it... baseball.

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:04.930
Isn't that obvious?

00:17:20.930 --> 00:17:22.320
I'm home!

00:17:23.440 --> 00:17:26.040
Papa, welcome home!

00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:26.040
Hey, Shingo.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:27.360
Welcome home.

00:17:27.360 --> 00:17:29.380
Goro's home too.

00:17:29.380 --> 00:17:30.490
I see.

00:17:33.550 --> 00:17:34.460
Hey!

00:17:34.460 --> 00:17:35.540
How're you feeling, Goro?

00:17:42.880 --> 00:17:45.350
What are you doing when you've just been discharged from the hospital?

00:17:45.350 --> 00:17:47.180
Can't you tell?

00:17:47.180 --> 00:17:50.040
I've been resting my lower body for so long...

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:52.350
that even if it's only my left leg, I want to strengthen it.

00:17:52.740 --> 00:17:54.050
Don't tell me...

00:17:54.050 --> 00:17:56.310
you're planning on playing in the tournament?

00:17:58.050 --> 00:17:59.520
So what if I am?

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:01.140
Don't do it!

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:05.490
Don't you know what kind of risk you're taking by being so reckless!?

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:09.320
Think about the future... No, right around the corner...

00:18:09.320 --> 00:18:11.450
About becoming a pro baseball player!

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:18.850
You should know that leg injuries are hard to recover from for pro baseball players!

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:20.810
Pro, huh?

00:18:21.750 --> 00:18:24.650
Compared to going up against Kaido,

00:18:24.650 --> 00:18:27.930
that is something I have absolutely no interest in right now.

00:18:30.300 --> 00:18:34.220
To defeat Kaido, where Toshiya and Mayumura are...

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:38.030
Right now, that's all I can think of.

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:02.580
All right, here it comes!

00:19:01.290 --> 00:19:02.580
{missing bg tl}

00:19:04.630 --> 00:19:05.740
{missing bg2}

00:19:05.740 --> 00:19:07.150
{missing bg3}

00:19:07.080 --> 00:19:10.380
Hattori used to be on the track team, right?{eventually md2 style if missing bg gets tld}

00:19:08.070 --> 00:19:10.220
{missing bg4}

00:19:10.220 --> 00:19:12.090
{missing bg5}

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:11.470
Yeah.

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:14.440
And, as expected, his athletic abilities are great.

00:19:12.090 --> 00:19:13.200
{missing bg6}

00:19:13.200 --> 00:19:14.240
{missing bg7}

00:19:14.440 --> 00:19:17.060
In just a week he's become a great shortstop.

00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:17.060
{missing bg8}

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:24.580
Taiga's being Taiga, being able to throw a curve in such a short time.

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:26.440
The newcomers this year...

00:19:26.840 --> 00:19:28.150
they're not cute at all.

00:19:29.970 --> 00:19:32.540
That guy's got a good form.

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:33.990
S-Shigeno!?

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:33.990
S-Shigeno!?

00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:39.110
You don't have to act so surprised!

00:19:39.110 --> 00:19:41.920
You're acting as if you just saw a ghost or an alien.

00:19:42.320 --> 00:19:45.520
N-No, it's your foot! Your foot!

00:19:45.520 --> 00:19:46.260
You... can walk already?

00:19:46.260 --> 00:19:47.380
You... can walk already?

00:19:47.930 --> 00:19:50.840
Oh, you mean this?

00:19:56.750 --> 00:19:57.560
No way...

00:19:57.560 --> 00:19:59.930
H-Hey! Stop it, Shigeno!

00:20:02.390 --> 00:20:03.960
Don't worry.

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:09.110
At this rate, I'll definitely be ready for the tournament that's a month away.

00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:13.960
Wait just a moment!

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:18.410
During this whole month, I've been throwing hundreds of pitches to perfect my form!

00:20:18.410 --> 00:20:21.180
What was all my hard work for!?

00:20:21.180 --> 00:20:25.050
Now, now. We all appreciate your hard work.

00:20:25.050 --> 00:20:28.650
But we can have as many pitchers as we want, right?

00:20:28.650 --> 00:20:30.930
Hey, Tashiro, can you crouch for a bit?

00:20:31.950 --> 00:20:33.090
What are you going to do?

00:20:33.910 --> 00:20:35.800
Pitching practice, of course.

00:20:36.230 --> 00:20:37.270
What!?

00:20:39.550 --> 00:20:41.400
If I don't start throwing again,

00:20:41.400 --> 00:20:44.350
I feel like I'm going to lose my pitching senses.

00:20:44.700 --> 00:20:46.420
Wait a minute, Shigeno.

00:20:46.420 --> 00:20:48.970
Aren't you rushing things a bit?

00:20:48.970 --> 00:20:50.230
With that leg, you still can't-

00:20:50.230 --> 00:20:52.130
It's fine, just crouch.

00:20:52.130 --> 00:20:55.530
I started warming my shoulder up yesterday.

00:20:56.020 --> 00:20:57.890
I don't care what happens next.

00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:00.800
Here I go.

00:21:13.420 --> 00:21:16.080
That's why I said it was too soon.

00:21:16.080 --> 00:21:18.230
You should just stop for today.

00:21:18.230 --> 00:21:19.230
Throw it back!

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:28.050
<i>I didn't sense anything wrong while I was warming up my shoulder.</i>

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:29.820
<i>What was with that strange feeling just now?</i>

00:21:34.450 --> 00:21:34.990
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

00:21:35.690 --> 00:21:36.450
<i>Don't tell me!?</i>

00:21:40.010 --> 00:21:41.080
Shigeno!

00:21:41.080 --> 00:21:42.410
Are you all right?

00:21:42.790 --> 00:21:44.970
Did you hurt your right leg again?

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:47.950
I'm going to run! 

00:21:47.950 --> 00:21:51.500
This cowardly lower body isn't my lower body!

00:21:52.590 --> 00:21:54.730
Hey! Shigeno!

00:21:55.970 --> 00:22:00.220
<i>This is bad! I wasn't taking the one month break seriously!</i>

00:22:00.220 --> 00:22:03.100
<i>If I don't rebuild my lower body first, then... </i>

00:22:04.020 --> 00:22:05.310
What did you say?

00:22:05.310 --> 00:22:09.400
In his head, he's only thinking about defeating Kaido.

00:22:12.910 --> 00:22:15.290
No matter what risks he has to take,

00:22:15.290 --> 00:22:17.820
he's definitely going to try and play in the tournament.

00:22:19.780 --> 00:22:23.490
So I have a favor to ask of you.

00:22:25.940 --> 00:22:29.170
Please don't put him in any of the games.

00:22:30.720 --> 00:22:35.130
Even if his condition seems great by the time the tournament starts.

00:22:36.800 --> 00:22:41.680
Like the time he broke his right shoulder and lost his place in the world...

00:22:44.080 --> 00:22:47.560
Goro, for him to lose baseball again... 

00:22:48.440 --> 00:22:51.310
I don't want to see that ever again.

00:24:41.590 --> 00:24:44.050
The summer tournament has finally started.

00:24:44.050 --> 00:24:45.970
Should I ignore my injury and play in the tournament,

00:24:45.970 --> 00:24:48.260
or trust my teammates and let them handle it?

00:24:48.260 --> 00:24:51.520
The troublesome first game's about to begin.

00:24:52.520 --> 00:24:53.850
Next time, on Major:

00:24:53.850 --> 00:24:55.100
Contagious Fighting Spirit.

00:24:55.510 --> 00:24:57.860
Run to the stage of your dreams!
